1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
In this tutorial, ms1, ms2, and ms3 are Docker profiles. I ask Chief to fix a sample duplicate-webhook bug.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Chief uses NVIDIA Nemotron Ultra through Nebius. I review Builder and Reviewer, their models, working folder, and team access.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,000
I apply the setup. Both specialists appear in Engineering with the approved model and Ask permissions.

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Chief’s accepted receipts link to both tasks. A follow-up here made the actual assignments happen.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
I open Builder’s returned tool output. The duplicate event produced two invoices where the test expected one.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Builder records event IDs and ignores repeats. All three regression tests now pass.

7
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Reviewer separately ran the same regression suite. Here is its returned output.

8
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:16,000
The review checks the actual handler diff and explains the sample’s limits: deduplication is held in memory.

9
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:25,000
I open Share group, start sharing, and create an invitation. Codes are hidden here.

10
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:35,000
On ms2, I paste that invitation and join. Each installation keeps its own copy of the conversation.

11
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,000
All three members now appear.

12
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,600
Now I send a message.

13
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:46,100
ms2 receives it and replies.

14
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:50,600
ms2 selects a bot, permitted people, and approval.

15
00:01:50,600 --> 00:02:02,300
I select ms2’s account under Run with and request the check. I supplied the patch separately; joining the group does not copy files.

16
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:11,300
On ms2, I review the request and approve it. The bot uses ms2’s own workspace.

17
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:20,300
Native tools still ask for approval. I use Allow once for these sample commands.

18
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:25,800
I open the completed result on ms1.

19
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:31,300
ms2 sees the same completed reply.

20
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:36,800
ms3 can read it too.

21
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:44,800
I keep the coding assignments, review evidence, and shared check available in their conversations.
